OL,3,GNEWSAHow Children in Need is helping
OL,4,Ayoung people grow in confidence
OL,5,
OL,6,FSeventeen-year-old Rachel has cared for
OL,7,Fher younger brother Reuben for seven
OL,8,Fyears.
OL,10,FAs her parents both work long hours for
OL,11,Fthe NHS, Rachel regularly looks after
OL,12,Fher 13-year-old brother, who has autism
OL,13,Fand learning difficulties.
OL,15,F"These caring responsibilities usually
OL,16,Fhappen at times like after school
OL,17,Ffrequently, during the weekends and
OL,18,Fsome school holidays," she said.
